 ## Background
-The method was proposed by researchers from Brigham and Women's Hospital, Harvard Medical School [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of adaptive filtering for image sequences and volumes [1, 3]. A similar technique was previously used to visualize strain-rate tensors in cardiac studies [2]. The method addresses the limitations of existing diffusion tensor visualization techniques, such as glyphs, streamlines, and line integral convolution, which suffer from occlusion, starting-point dependency, and issues with non-linear diffusion [S1, unofficial].
